---
/**
 * The /activity headline (docs/projects/redesign/design-export-remaining/design_handoff_activity,
 * band 1).
 *
 * THE HERO STATEMENT IS NOT THE EXPORT'S. The revised export says "Every request this site
 * receives, and what asked for it.", and design-export-remaining/README.md says that line must not
 * ship: the store logs two event classes, agent-surface fetches and pages served as Markdown, and
 * it does not log page views. The wording here is the honest scope, taken from the shape of the
 * data rather than from the mockup.
 *
 * THE STAMP IS THE ONLY LIVENESS CUE, and it reads at hour resolution because hour resolution is
 * all the store has. There is no pulsing dot, no polling and no "live" indicator; the bundle says
 * "there must never be one". The page ships no JavaScript at all, as of 2026-08-29: the one script
 * the document used to carry localised the legacy tree's stamp in the browser, and it went with
 * that tree. This stamp is not localised — it is labelled UTC and is true with scripting off,
 * which is what the rest of the page's UTC framing needs it to be.
 *
 * THE STAMP IS SPELLED, THE MACHINE SURFACES STAY ISO. The bundle writes it "22 Aug 2026, 06:08
 * UTC". `utcStamp()` in the summary module keeps its ISO-shaped form for
 * /activity.md, and /activity.json and every `datetime` attribute are ISO too.
 *
 * THE HERO'S TYPE AND LAYOUT ARE `.rd-hero` IN global.css: the H1, the 32ch lede, the row, the
 * right block's hairline shell and the 720px collapse. The stamp sat in a 320px grid column beside
 * the lede until 2026-09-05, with its own 900px stack and a left-rule-to-top-rule swap; it now
 * sits on the shell's right edge, where every page's right block sits.
 *
 * IT CARRIES `data-module='activity-hero'` AND NO `.modern-skin`, since 2026-08-29: this is the
 * only /activity hero in the document and retro restyles it in place, under that module prefix in
 * src/styles/retro.css. The prefix is load-bearing — Astro appends a `[data-astro-cid-…]` to the
 * selectors below and that attribute counts as a class, so a retro rule without it loses silently.
 */
interface Props {
  renderedAt: Date;
}

const { renderedAt } = Astro.props;

const stamp = new Intl.DateTimeFormat('en-GB', {
  day: 'numeric',
  month: 'short',
  year: 'numeric',
  hour: '2-digit',
  minute: '2-digit',
  timeZone: 'UTC',
  timeZoneName: 'short',
});
---

{/*
  A div, not a section — the same call every other redesigned hero made: `npm run validate:html`
  names an h1 inside sectioning content, and an unnamed <section> is not exposed as a region.
*/}
<div class="rd-section rd-hero activity-hero" data-module="activity-hero">
  <h1><span class="rd-fill">Activity</span></h1>

  <div class="hero-row">
    <p class="hero-statement">
      Agent surfaces fetched, pages served as Markdown, and what asked for them.
    </p>
    <div class="hero-aside hero-stamp">
      <span class="stamp-rendered">Rendered {stamp.format(renderedAt)}</span>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<style>
  .activity-hero { padding-top: 72px; }

  .stamp-rendered {
    font-size: 18px;
    color: var(--ink-2);
  }

  @media (max-width: 720px) {
    .activity-hero { padding-top: 52px; }
  }
</style>
